  "strategy": "Approach and Rationale\nThe Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem involves finding a step function h:[0,2]\u2192[0,1] with integral 1 that minimizes the maximum overlap with its shifts. This non-convex, high-dimensional search space requires escaping local minima. My approach uses guided basin hopping with repair operations, where mutations drive solutions toward improving lags while dynamic repairs maintain constraints. This differs from local searches (Simulated Annealing/PSO) by combining targeted mutations with efficient repairs, ensuring integral constraints without penalty terms. The method leverages parent guidance for initialization and focuses on lag-based objectives to escape suboptimal regions faster.",
